# mcp__something_new — something/something_new

Makes a space in the spaces folder as `something new <name>` does, from the empty template or, with `from`, from one of something's templates (AGENTS.md in the spaces folder lists them), and returns what it printed. Use this tool instead of running `something new` in the shell.

## Schema
```ts
type Args = {
  /** The template to start from, by its name: agents, for instance. */
  from?: string;
  /** The new space's name: lowercase letters, digits and -. */
  name: string;
};
```
Execute by writing JSON to xd://mcp__something_new.

